  "content": {
    "id": "p30-p4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "[Triangle inequality]\n\nThe cosine rule states that\n$$\\cos A=\\frac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2bc},$$\nwhere $A\\ne0$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-p4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $b^2+c^2-a^2<2bc$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Since $0^\\circ<A<180^\\circ$, $\\cos A<1$. Thus $b^2+c^2-a^2=2bc\\cos A<2bc$.",
          "worked": "For an interior angle of a triangle, $0^\\circ<A<180^\\circ$, so $\\cos A<1$. Also, $b,c>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2bc}&<1\\\\b^2+c^2-a^2&<2bc.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-p4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that $b<a+c$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(b-c)^2<a^2$, so $|b-c|<a$. Hence $b-c<a$, giving $b<a+c$.",
          "worked": "From (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2+c^2-a^2&<2bc\\\\b^2-2bc+c^2&<a^2\\\\(b-c)^2&<a^2\\\\|b-c|&<a.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $b-c\\leq|b-c|$,\n$$\\begin{align*}b-c&<a\\\\b&<a+c.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-p4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What does this say about the side lengths of triangles in general?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The sum of any two side lengths of a triangle is strictly greater than the third side length.",
          "worked": "The same reasoning applies whichever side is labelled $b$. Thus $a<b+c$, $b<a+c$ and $c<a+b$: any two side lengths sum to more than the third.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
